{"id":3204,"date":"2017-01-31T20:31:08","date_gmt":"2017-02-01T03:31:08","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=3204"},"modified":"2017-01-31T20:31:08","modified_gmt":"2017-02-01T03:31:08","slug":"quartzfest-ham-radio-convention-in-the-sanoran-desert","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/01\/31\/quartzfest-ham-radio-convention-in-the-sanoran-desert\/","title":{"rendered":"Quartzfest &#8211; Ham Radio Convention In The Sanoran Desert"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>There were two reasons for our trip to Quartzsite, AZ this past week. \u00a0The first was because we were so close (3+ hours) drive time from there we just HAD to see what everyone has been going to see and do for so many years, (<a href=\"http:\/\/www.quartzsitervshow.com\/\">The big Vacation, Sports, and RV Show<\/a>).<\/p>\n<p>Then I found out that this week was also the 20th annual Amateur Radio Convention known as &#8220;<a href=\"http:\/\/quartzfest.org\/\">Quartzfest<\/a>&#8220;. \u00a0Being a ham radio operator since the late &#8217;60&#8217;s, (My call is WB8BHK) I thought it would be fun to hang out with some like-minded people. \u00a0We were all camping in the same area &#8230; on BLM land about 6 miles south of Quartzsite in an area known as &#8220;Road Runner&#8221;. \u00a0Quartzsite is just above Yuma on this map.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_3233\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-3233\" style=\"width: 258px\" class=\"wp-caption alignright\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/sonoran_desert.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-3233\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/sonoran_desert-300x173.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"258\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/sonoran_desert-300x173.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/sonoran_desert.jpg 550w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 258px) 100vw, 258px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-3233\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Sonoran Desert<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Camping in the desert there is free for up to 14 days. \u00a0Of course, you need to be totally self-contained (fresh water\/waste tanks\/batteries\/generator\/solar) since you are in the desert with no utilities or hookups. \u00a0When we showed up on Sunday, the registration desk showed we were rig #239 &#8230; by the time we left on Thursday there were just under 600 rigs\/hams registered!<\/p>\n<p>The purpose of the Quartzfest Convention is to provide a time for education (through seminars and forums), sharing of ideas, display and demonstration of radios and antenna projects, and of course &#8212; to have fun.<\/p>\n<p>The Sonoran desert treated us well while we were there, although Monday was VERY windy. \u00a0Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday were beautiful sunny days with low winds and temps in the 50&#8217;s to 60&#8217;s.<\/p>\n<p>The pictures in the slide show below illustrate just some of what we saw surrounding us in the desert. \u00a0Some of the interesting RV rigs with all kinds of antennas. \u00a0 Check out the pix of the guy in his electric recumbant bicycle, he was zipping around all week silently. \u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.backcountryrecumbentcycles.com\/\">Take a look at Mark&#8217;s company web site here.<\/a><\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-3204 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-full'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-07.49.20.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-07.49.20.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-3208\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-07.49.20.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-07.49.20-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-07.49.20-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-07.49.20-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-3208'>\n\t\t\t\tSunrise in the Sonoran Desert\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.28.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.28.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-3209\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.28.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.28-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.28-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.28-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-3209'>\n\t\t\t\tCampers around us\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.31.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.31.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-3210\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/01\/2017-01-23-08.03.3